cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "An Explicit Rate for the Logarithmic Exponent of the Walsh–Hadamard Transform"
authors:
  - family-names: "Silva Ortiz"
    given-names: "Javier"
    email: "javier@epistemic.one"
    affiliation: "Epistemic One"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7076-0863"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24575295"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jsilvao/walsh-hadamard-explicit-rate"
abstract: >-
  Paper and Lean 4 development. Over every field of characteristic zero,
  the Walsh–Hadamard transform on N = 2^k points has binary linear circuits
  with C(H^{⊗k}) ≤ 2^k (1+k)^{1/2 + 200·√(log₂ℓ/ℓ)} gates whenever
  ℓ = ⌊log₂⌊log₂(1+k)⌋⌋ ≥ 48, that is,
  N (log N)^{1/2 + O(√(log⁽⁴⁾N / log⁽³⁾N))}. This makes explicit the o(1)
  in OpenAI's N (log N)^{1/2+o(1)} for this transform. The paper also
  sharpens one level of OpenAI's template and proves limits of the method.
  Every theorem, proposition, lemma and corollary is machine-checked in
  Lean 4 (104 results, standard axioms only).
keywords:
  - Walsh–Hadamard transform
  - linear circuits
  - fast Fourier transform
  - Lean
  - formal verification
